# Router variant of omarchy-iso/builder/archinstall.packages: the package set
# pacstrap installs into the target before the Omarchy runtime, and the seed of
# the ISO's offline mirror.
#
# Identical to profile/server/archinstall.packages. The router profile differs
# from the server profile in its core list (omarchy-router.packages: nftables
# instead of ufw, plus wireguard-tools) and in its setup tree (install/router/),
# not in what pacstrap lays down first. Kept as its own file rather than a
# symlink so the two profiles stay independently editable.
#
# Differences from the desktop list are the server ones:
#   - dropped: pipewire, alsa-firmware, sof-firmware (no audio stack).
#   - dropped: base-devel (no compiler in the base; `omarchy-server-addon dev`
#     brings it back).
#   - dropped: tailscale (bundled through the `tailscale` addon instead).
#   - added: nano (`base` ships no editor).
#
# This file only seeds the offline mirror; the packages that must land in the
# target are in omarchy-router.packages, which the orchestrator reads back.
#
# Both microcode packages stay: the mirror must be able to serve either CPU.
amd-ucode
base
efibootmgr
intel-ucode
limine
linux
linux-firmware
nano
omarchy-keyring
openssh
snapper
